<section id="safety" class="city-section" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
  <div class="safety-inner">
    <h2 id="safety-title">What keeps workers in line</h2>
    <ol class="safety-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Worktrees:</strong> every worker edits its own git worktree and branch; nothing reaches your branch until the orchestrator re-runs the tests and merges.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shell allowlist:</strong> opencode workers may only run test and build runners and read-only commands; everything else is denied.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Edits stay inside the worktree:</strong> file edits outside it are denied (shell runners are not covered, so this is a guard, not a sandbox).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Circuit breaker:</strong> a worker that keeps hitting denied commands or failing tool calls is stopped and handed back to the orchestrator.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No secrets to cold workers:</strong> auth, secrets and data work stays on Claude subagents; <code>.env</code> files are never copied into a worktree.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Guards, not a sandbox:</strong> in Claude Code the guard hooks block obvious writes and fetch-and-run commands; a test runner can still run any code in your project.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="safety-source">Every claim here is in <code>scripts/agy-task</code> and <code>claude/hooks/guard.py</code>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

